      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those platitudes, though well-intentioned, can feel dismissive when you are in the depth of grief. It is valid to feel like a piece of you is missing because a huge part of your life was tied to him. Your feelings of meaninglessness are a direct reflection of how much he meant to you, and that void is real. Allow yourself to feel this immense pain right now; it is part of the process, even if it doesn't feel like it will pass.",
      "source": "target",
